  "instructions": [
    "Heat 2 tbsp of vegetable oil in a Donabe over medium heat.",
    "Add 1 small onion and cook until softened, about 3 minutes.",
    "Mince 2 cloves of garlic and 1 small piece of ginger, and add to the Donabe.",
    "Mix in 2 tsp of Tom Yum paste and cook for 1 minute.",
    "Add 4 oz of coconut milk and stir well.",
    "Add 1 tsp of sugar-free sweetener, 1 tsp of fish sauce, 2 tbsp of lime juice, 1 tsp of tamarind paste, and 0.5 tsp of crushed red pepper. Mix well.",
    "Add 4 oz of Braeburn apples, peeled and cored, to the Donabe.",
    "Add 4 oz of fish fillet, cut into small pieces.",
    "Season with salt to taste.",
    "Cook for an additional 3-4 minutes, or until the fish is cooked through and the apples are tender.",
    "Stir in a handful of fresh cilantro and serve hot.",
    "Garnish with additional cilantro and serve with steamed rice or noodles, if desired.",
    "Let the dish rest for 5 minutes before serving to allow the flavors to meld together.",
    "Serve immediately and enjoy!"
